WEBVTT

00:58.475 --> 01:00.101
Atmospheric instability is

01:00.185 --> 01:03.063
the collision of two types of air
with different properties.

02:02.789 --> 02:03.748
I'm late.

02:19.889 --> 02:20.890
Wait for me.

02:21.516 --> 02:23.643
- No, you leave later.
- But aren't we late?

02:23.726 --> 02:25.103
No, you are.

02:33.027 --> 02:34.362
THE EFFECTIVENESS OF FOG ADVISORIES
AND CASES FROM ABROAD

02:57.719 --> 02:58.761
Hello?

03:26.497 --> 03:28.374
So what do you want me to do?

03:28.917 --> 03:31.586
No. I won't do it anymore.

03:31.669 --> 03:33.546
There's nothing I can do for you!

03:34.339 --> 03:36.174
Never call me again.

03:48.019 --> 03:52.899
When cold air suddenly meets warm air…

03:56.444 --> 03:58.488
I left the USB.

03:59.197 --> 04:00.114
Right.

04:02.825 --> 04:04.911
I was going to bring it to you.

04:07.872 --> 04:08.706
Thanks.

04:11.125 --> 04:13.127
By the way, who was that?

04:17.215 --> 04:18.967
Someone I used to know.

04:22.762 --> 04:26.766
…the atmosphere becomes unstable
and dangerous weather occurs.

04:28.977 --> 04:31.312
Aren't you late for work? You better go.

04:31.896 --> 04:33.398
Yes, I will.

04:37.068 --> 04:38.278
Wait for me.

04:42.824 --> 04:44.951
Where are you going?
I want to talk to you.

04:45.034 --> 04:46.202
Later.

04:51.541 --> 04:53.376
Do you usually hold grudges?

04:53.960 --> 04:54.836
"Grudges"?

04:56.421 --> 04:58.172
Did you just say "grudges"?

04:58.256 --> 05:00.216
Yes, I dated Si-woo.

05:00.300 --> 05:02.802
I met him for the first time
at the Metropolitan Office,

05:02.885 --> 05:04.554
and we went out for a few months.

05:04.637 --> 05:06.889
So what? What else do you want to know?

05:06.973 --> 05:10.435
My crush in college
and my first love in high school?

05:10.518 --> 05:12.562
You aren't getting the point.

05:12.645 --> 05:15.315
Do you think I'm mad
because of your ex-boyfriend?

05:15.398 --> 05:16.399
Aren't you?

05:16.482 --> 05:17.734
You said you didn't know him.

05:17.817 --> 05:19.527
You said you had never seen him.

05:19.610 --> 05:21.237
Why did you lie to me?

05:21.821 --> 05:25.616
I didn't want you to feel uncomfortable
when you saw him at work.

05:25.700 --> 05:26.993
Because I hate

05:27.076 --> 05:29.787
seeing her face
whenever I go to Headquarters.

05:29.871 --> 05:31.956
Do you think I've been okay with it?

05:32.999 --> 05:35.626
I told you I had a fiancée
from the beginning.

05:35.710 --> 05:38.421
You're the one who said
you didn't care about the past.

05:40.381 --> 05:41.215
I see.

05:42.425 --> 05:44.677
Is that why your past came to our wedding

05:44.761 --> 05:46.846
and made a scene?

05:50.600 --> 05:51.434
Forget it.

05:54.395 --> 05:56.397
We're not done talking.

05:56.981 --> 05:59.275
If I don't leave now,
I'll be late for work.

05:59.358 --> 06:01.319
I have to sort out
the mess you made yesterday.

06:02.653 --> 06:03.863
But…

06:23.466 --> 06:26.719
The weather is warm compared to
the average temperature of early June.

06:26.803 --> 06:30.139
Today will be hot
as the temperature suddenly rises.

06:30.223 --> 06:32.100
Currently, Seoul is 23°C

06:32.183 --> 06:34.018
and Incheon is 21°C,

06:34.102 --> 06:36.187
which is about 1 or 2°C
lower than yesterday,

06:36.270 --> 06:39.273
but the midday temperature will be 29°C.

06:39.357 --> 06:40.483
Considering that June is

06:40.566 --> 06:43.444
the beginning of summer,
the weather is still hot.

06:43.528 --> 06:45.279
The skies will be clear all day.

06:45.363 --> 06:48.741
Strong sunlight will shine down
through cloudless skies,

06:48.825 --> 06:50.409
so please be wary of UV rays…

06:50.493 --> 06:52.662
Keep both hands on the wheel.

06:53.663 --> 06:55.081
I can drive with one hand.

06:56.457 --> 06:58.501
I want you to drive safely.

06:59.877 --> 07:01.003
Okay.

07:02.755 --> 07:04.465
Different principles.

07:08.177 --> 07:09.846
CHAE YU-JIN

07:12.348 --> 07:13.766
CHAE YU-JIN

07:15.143 --> 07:15.977
Well…

07:16.060 --> 07:17.895
I have to drive safely.

07:17.979 --> 07:19.188
Right?

07:22.150 --> 07:24.026
Different wounds.

07:29.615 --> 07:34.662
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

07:38.708 --> 07:40.418
Drop me off at the crosswalk.

07:40.960 --> 07:42.336
Why? We're almost there.

07:42.420 --> 07:43.671
Let's just go.

07:43.754 --> 07:44.922
Drop me off.

07:45.006 --> 07:46.299
Are you afraid we'll be seen?

07:46.382 --> 07:48.801
We can say we met on the way by chance.

07:48.885 --> 07:50.428
Should I get out here?

07:51.721 --> 07:55.433
Just as cold air suddenly meets
a mass of warm air,

07:55.933 --> 07:59.312
you and I have met with our differences.

08:02.940 --> 08:03.858
Okay.

08:04.484 --> 08:06.402
- I'll drop you off there.
- Okay.

08:06.486 --> 08:08.446
Take a right…

08:12.283 --> 08:13.201
What?

08:15.328 --> 08:16.412
Hey.

08:26.380 --> 08:28.049
We've already decided to begin.

08:29.509 --> 08:33.012
How many abnormal climate events
caused by this decision

08:33.638 --> 08:35.848
will we be able to avoid?

08:36.432 --> 08:43.022
EPISODE 5
LOCALIZED HEAVY RAIN

08:49.278 --> 08:51.197
Let it slide.

08:55.076 --> 08:57.119
- We met on our way here.
- Pardon?

08:58.037 --> 09:00.790
Forecaster Lee and I met
on the way here coincidentally.

09:01.832 --> 09:03.084
Okay.

09:03.751 --> 09:05.336
It was a coincidence.

09:10.800 --> 09:13.844
Traffic in Uijeongbu
has been congested all morning

09:13.928 --> 09:16.722
because the overflow
of Jungnang Stream flooded the roads.

09:17.306 --> 09:19.308
Flooded? Jungnang Stream?

09:19.850 --> 09:21.811
It rained in Uijeongbu overnight.

09:21.894 --> 09:23.437
It poured 50mm per hour.

09:23.521 --> 09:24.772
- Rain?
- Rain?

09:27.817 --> 09:28.901
Okay.

09:30.194 --> 09:32.113
But isn't it too early

09:32.780 --> 09:35.283
for localized heavy rain to fall?

09:35.366 --> 09:38.828
In terms of development,
it's a typical localized heavy rain.

09:38.911 --> 09:40.871
It took exactly 21 minutes

09:40.955 --> 09:44.584
for the rain cloud developed
in Uijeongbu to move to Namyangju.

09:44.667 --> 09:47.211
A heavy rain advisory was issued
around 5:30 a.m.

09:47.295 --> 09:50.256
The total accumulated precipitation
is predicted to be 70 to 80mm.

09:50.339 --> 09:52.675
Where's the precipitation concentrated?

09:52.758 --> 09:54.594
Near the Jungnang Stream footbridge.

09:54.677 --> 09:56.554
Jungnang Stream? My goodness.

09:56.637 --> 09:59.432
By the time the warning was issued,
it was already too late.

10:00.099 --> 10:02.059
- Yes.
- Okay.

10:02.685 --> 10:05.313
Director Jin. What do you think?

10:05.396 --> 10:08.441
Don't you think
the water vapor inflow is abnormally high?

10:08.524 --> 10:10.318
Yesterday's daytime temperature

10:10.401 --> 10:13.571
rose to 30°C and caused
the heating of the earth's surface.

10:13.654 --> 10:17.950
As a result, the atmosphere
became more unstable.

10:18.034 --> 10:20.870
The decisive reason
seems to be the instability

10:20.953 --> 10:23.247
in the vicinity of Uijeongbu
as cold air descended

10:23.331 --> 10:24.707
from the north overnight.

10:24.790 --> 10:25.875
What?

10:25.958 --> 10:27.043
On what grounds?

10:27.668 --> 10:29.086
If you look here,

10:29.629 --> 10:32.214
the temperature difference
between the upper and lower layers

10:32.298 --> 10:34.300
of the atmosphere
near Uijeongbu is almost 40.

10:37.803 --> 10:38.638
I see.

10:39.263 --> 10:40.264
- Director Jin.
- Yes.

10:40.348 --> 10:41.891
Analyze this in detail.

10:42.558 --> 10:43.434
Yes, sir.

10:45.895 --> 10:48.356
Very sharp. Good job.

10:48.898 --> 10:51.901
- I'm glad to have you at Headquarters.
- Thank you.

10:54.403 --> 10:56.113
All right.

10:59.659 --> 11:01.619
Of all those rain echoes,

11:01.702 --> 11:04.664
how do you know which one
will develop into a localized rain?

11:04.747 --> 11:05.915
How do you find it in an hour?

11:06.832 --> 11:09.251
Let's say you're boiling water in a pot.

11:09.335 --> 11:11.754
It's similar to guessing

11:11.837 --> 11:14.090
where the bubbles will come up first.

11:14.173 --> 11:15.174
What?

11:16.425 --> 11:18.511
Don't try to guess

11:18.594 --> 11:20.346
if you want to stay sane.

11:23.849 --> 11:25.393
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

11:25.476 --> 11:26.644
All right.

11:27.686 --> 11:29.230
Don't be intimidated.

11:29.313 --> 11:30.648
Think of it as a jab

11:30.731 --> 11:33.150
thrown by the man up there
to keep us alert.

11:33.234 --> 11:34.193
Okay?

11:34.860 --> 11:37.655
Keep your eyes wide open
and monitor the situation.

11:40.116 --> 11:42.618
Real-time monitoring is the key
to localized heavy rain.

11:43.411 --> 11:44.412
That's all.

11:44.495 --> 11:45.955
Okay. Good work.

11:46.038 --> 11:48.165
- Thank you.
- Good work.

11:48.249 --> 11:49.291
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

11:50.918 --> 11:52.545
- Hello.
- Hi.

11:53.379 --> 11:55.005
I'm sorry. I'm late.

11:56.841 --> 11:58.759
- Senior Forecaster Um.
- Yes, sir.

12:02.596 --> 12:03.848
Let's have some coffee.

12:05.099 --> 12:06.851
- Oh, okay.
- Come.

12:07.476 --> 12:08.477
Yes, sir.

12:22.700 --> 12:23.534
Thank you.

12:24.577 --> 12:27.455
Didn't you go home
after drinking with me last night?

12:27.538 --> 12:31.375
I couldn't sleep, so I had another drink.

12:32.126 --> 12:34.753
- So I slept in.
- This is so unexpected.

12:34.837 --> 12:36.297
The great Um Dong-han drinking

12:36.380 --> 12:39.467
and being late during
the summer disaster prevention period.

12:44.305 --> 12:45.139
What's wrong?

12:46.307 --> 12:49.935
The climate pattern changes
every three days.

12:50.019 --> 12:52.062
I'm bound to change too.

12:53.689 --> 12:55.065
Is everything okay at home?

12:57.443 --> 12:58.694
Everything is fine.

13:04.575 --> 13:06.160
You were crazy about the weather

13:06.744 --> 13:08.996
that you were always
at sea or in the mountains.

13:09.079 --> 13:10.789
You were so busy

13:10.873 --> 13:12.875
that you'd only come home
every now and then.

13:12.958 --> 13:15.085
And the next morning, you'd be off again.

13:15.169 --> 13:16.837
Were you ever there for Bo-mi?

13:16.921 --> 13:17.922
Were you?

13:19.298 --> 13:21.133
That was how Bo-mi and I lived

13:22.134 --> 13:23.928
for the past 14 years.

13:24.762 --> 13:26.180
Do you get that, Dong-han?

13:53.999 --> 13:55.042
What?

13:55.960 --> 13:57.253
Are you going somewhere?

13:59.129 --> 14:00.214
Well…

14:01.131 --> 14:02.841
I'll be staying at Headquarters.

14:04.426 --> 14:07.221
I have a lot of work during
summer disaster prevention period.

14:08.222 --> 14:09.765
Do you really have to do this?

14:10.474 --> 14:12.601
You and Bo-mi will be more comfortable.

14:12.685 --> 14:13.978
Do whatever you want.

14:14.478 --> 14:16.522
Why did you even come back
in the first place?

14:59.231 --> 15:01.567
Does Senior Forecaster Um like to drink?

15:01.650 --> 15:04.570
I don't know. I never heard he did.

15:05.154 --> 15:08.782
I guess he's having a hard time
because he didn't get promoted.

15:08.866 --> 15:10.034
Right?

15:11.285 --> 15:12.286
Don't you think so?

15:13.037 --> 15:14.121
I'm not sure.

15:14.705 --> 15:15.873
Attention, everyone.

15:16.749 --> 15:17.917
We'll analyze the issues

15:18.000 --> 15:20.461
related to localized heavy rain
over the past ten years

15:20.544 --> 15:23.589
including precipitation, duration,
and distribution by region.

15:23.672 --> 15:24.840
The past ten years?

15:24.924 --> 15:25.841
Yes.

15:27.635 --> 15:29.929
Do we need to look at the past ten years?

15:30.512 --> 15:32.681
This morning was an unusual case.

15:32.765 --> 15:34.350
It was,

15:34.433 --> 15:37.227
but a similar pattern may be repeated
due to climate change.

15:37.311 --> 15:39.480
We need to analyze it
from a long-term perspective.

15:39.563 --> 15:41.315
It's a time of high uncertainty.

15:41.398 --> 15:43.067
Analyzing it short-term

15:43.150 --> 15:44.610
will be more helpful

15:44.693 --> 15:47.029
in forecasting weather more accurately.

15:47.112 --> 15:50.074
Right. The Director General said
real-time monitoring was the key.

15:50.157 --> 15:53.577
Isn't real-time monitoring
more important than analyzing data?

16:06.757 --> 16:09.343
Please analyze the data
from the past ten years.

16:13.931 --> 16:15.724
I guess I'm working overtime again.

16:43.293 --> 16:44.461
HOW ACCURATE IS THE RAIN FORECAST?

16:44.545 --> 16:46.755
- Did you check?
- I'll call them now.

16:47.965 --> 16:49.425
What's this?

16:49.508 --> 16:51.468
Why aren't the stories unified?

16:51.552 --> 16:54.430
We found out after
the heavy rain advisory was issued.

16:54.513 --> 16:55.764
Some wrote the articles

16:55.848 --> 16:57.766
before we put out the press release.

16:58.934 --> 17:00.310
Darn it.

17:01.687 --> 17:04.314
- Which team is in charge?
- They probably changed shifts.

17:05.774 --> 17:06.942
Now it's Chief Team Two.

17:07.026 --> 17:08.652
Chief Team Two?

17:12.698 --> 17:15.284
TREAT THE SKIES AS A FRIEND
AND THE PEOPLE AS THE SKIES

17:15.367 --> 17:17.286
Chief Team Two.

17:18.996 --> 17:21.206
Chief Team Two.

17:23.917 --> 17:26.587
Chief Team Two.

17:31.467 --> 17:32.968
FORECAST TRAINING

17:43.020 --> 17:45.564
- He called.
- Who called?

17:54.782 --> 17:56.283
It's over between us.

17:56.366 --> 17:57.868
Why is he calling me?

17:57.951 --> 17:59.119
I'm sorry.

18:00.037 --> 18:01.497
Please block him.

18:01.580 --> 18:03.916
I'm already in deep trouble
because of you.

18:03.999 --> 18:05.209
Because of me?

18:05.292 --> 18:06.627
Ki-jun found out

18:07.544 --> 18:08.796
that we had dated.

18:08.879 --> 18:10.798
It's all in the past. Why is it a problem?

18:12.216 --> 18:14.635
Why did you make a scene at my wedding?

18:14.718 --> 18:17.012
And why did you
get dispatched to Headquarters

18:17.096 --> 18:18.972
after I returned from my honeymoon?

18:19.890 --> 18:21.850
It's obvious Ki-jun thinks it's weird.

18:26.563 --> 18:27.523
So?

18:28.607 --> 18:29.733
Did you guys fight?

18:31.652 --> 18:33.070
Did he hassle you?

18:35.405 --> 18:37.366
Ki-jun isn't like that.

18:37.991 --> 18:39.159
He cares for me a lot.

18:40.035 --> 18:42.579
He'd never hold grudges
over something like that.

18:43.664 --> 18:45.666
Okay. Got it. I'll be careful.

18:45.749 --> 18:46.875
Do you have more to say?

18:46.959 --> 18:48.252
No, I don't.

18:52.506 --> 18:53.340
Ki-jun.

19:05.769 --> 19:07.062
What are you doing?

19:07.688 --> 19:08.772
We were talking.

19:09.439 --> 19:10.649
I mean,

19:11.692 --> 19:15.237
Chief Team shouldn't deal
with the press directly.

19:15.320 --> 19:17.656
You have to go through
the Office of Spokesperson.

19:18.991 --> 19:21.994
This is why the press releases
different stories.

19:22.077 --> 19:23.287
Isn't it?

19:23.370 --> 19:24.997
Talk to me, Ki-jun.

19:25.080 --> 19:26.915
- I'll explain.
- Stay out of this, Reporter Chae.

19:26.999 --> 19:28.083
This is internal business.

19:29.751 --> 19:31.795
Why are you doing this?

19:31.879 --> 19:34.298
A rookie may not know this,

19:34.381 --> 19:36.216
but the Office of Spokesperson
is the voice of KMA.

19:36.300 --> 19:39.219
If you don't cooperate
with the spokesperson,

19:39.303 --> 19:42.431
the information is bound to be different
like in the articles this morning.

19:42.514 --> 19:44.600
Exactly. If there had been
good communication

19:44.683 --> 19:47.728
between the Office of Spokesperson
and the reporters,

19:47.811 --> 19:50.272
the Chief Team wouldn't have to intervene.

19:50.355 --> 19:52.441
Start sharing information properly first.

19:53.150 --> 19:55.527
Who said you could
keep crossing lines like that?

19:55.611 --> 19:58.197
You've been working here for a long time,
so you must know this.

19:58.280 --> 20:00.407
The Situation Room is the heart of KMA.

20:01.491 --> 20:04.369
Do you know of a heart
that asks for permission to beat?

20:05.037 --> 20:06.163
What?

20:09.041 --> 20:11.627
If you want a real-time report
on severe weather,

20:11.710 --> 20:12.961
come to the Situation Room

20:13.045 --> 20:15.339
and monitor it yourself every time.

20:55.963 --> 20:57.172
What's up with that guy?

20:57.756 --> 20:59.800
Was it wrong of the Office of Spokesperson

20:59.883 --> 21:03.095
to ask him to share
severe weather conditions?

21:03.178 --> 21:04.221
Also…

21:04.304 --> 21:07.474
how dare he talk privately to a reporter,
a married woman at that?

21:07.557 --> 21:09.393
What a brazen punk.

21:10.227 --> 21:11.937
How dare he talk to my wife

21:13.188 --> 21:16.275
standing face to face
in the middle of KMA?

21:16.942 --> 21:17.859
You found out.

21:19.027 --> 21:19.945
Found out what?

21:20.654 --> 21:22.990
That Si-woo is Yu-jin's ex-boyfriend.

21:24.825 --> 21:27.411
- Did you know that?
- Yes.

21:27.494 --> 21:29.621
- Since when?
- Since he was dispatched.

21:31.373 --> 21:33.709
You knew that and you took him in?

21:33.792 --> 21:35.919
Director Jin.
You shouldn't have done that.

21:36.003 --> 21:38.422
You went out with Yu-jin
knowing that you shouldn't.

21:38.505 --> 21:39.589
Well, you…

21:44.761 --> 21:47.889
Hey, do you know that you're really scary?

21:48.432 --> 21:49.266
What?

21:49.349 --> 21:52.102
Did you want to see
how I would react if I saw him?

21:52.185 --> 21:54.229
Is that how you wanted to get back at me?

21:54.313 --> 21:55.480
What are you saying?

21:56.440 --> 21:58.692
I guess that's how
you wanted to harass me.

21:58.775 --> 22:01.236
But you know what? I'm not that weak.

22:01.320 --> 22:03.655
I'm not the kind of person
who reacts sensitively

22:03.739 --> 22:05.324
to things like that.

22:06.199 --> 22:08.952
- Ki-jun, stop making--
- Wait a minute.

22:10.329 --> 22:11.246
Are you…

22:13.623 --> 22:15.042
still not over me?

22:17.794 --> 22:20.172
Come on, Ha-kyung. This is wrong.

22:20.756 --> 22:22.758
Why did you bring him to Headquarters?

22:23.675 --> 22:25.218
I'm already married.

22:25.302 --> 22:27.262
I can't get back together with--

22:30.640 --> 22:34.394
Gosh, I can't believe I have to deal
with this stupid son of a…

22:34.478 --> 22:37.773
Call me outside like this
one more time and I'll make

22:37.856 --> 22:40.317
an official complaint
to the Office of Spokesperson

22:40.400 --> 22:42.235
and have you be reprimanded,
Deputy Director Han.

22:42.319 --> 22:43.737
- Understood?
- Yes.

22:51.453 --> 22:52.788
I knew it.

22:53.622 --> 22:55.665
She isn't over me yet.

22:57.042 --> 22:58.126
Darn it.

22:59.252 --> 23:01.838
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

23:20.690 --> 23:21.733
Director Jin.

23:21.817 --> 23:24.027
I collected the cases
of heavy rain that caused great damage.

23:24.111 --> 23:25.237
Okay. Leave it there.

23:26.196 --> 23:27.197
Here?

23:32.410 --> 23:34.162
Would you like something to drink?

23:34.788 --> 23:35.747
No, thanks.

23:38.208 --> 23:39.876
Are you mad at me?

23:45.215 --> 23:47.759
- What do you mean?
- I think you are.

23:48.343 --> 23:52.013
Did I upset you
by commenting on your opinion

23:52.681 --> 23:54.766
in front of the Director General?

23:55.684 --> 23:57.102
Look, Forecaster Lee.

24:07.821 --> 24:08.655
Follow me.

24:20.500 --> 24:23.420
Why did he have to show off
in front of the Director General?

24:24.337 --> 24:25.338
Because of him,

24:25.422 --> 24:27.883
- we have to go through so much--
- Enough.

24:27.966 --> 24:30.635
Stop whining and keep analyzing.

24:47.110 --> 24:48.695
Forecaster Lee, you--

24:54.993 --> 24:56.536
What are you doing?

24:56.620 --> 24:58.413
Don't worry. We won't get caught.

24:59.414 --> 25:00.790
Is this why you provoked me?

25:01.958 --> 25:03.168
I didn't provoke you.

25:03.752 --> 25:06.087
I was really worried about you.

25:07.672 --> 25:09.841
Keep a distance
of a meter from me at work.

25:09.925 --> 25:10.842
It's an order.

25:16.932 --> 25:19.017
What did you and Ki-jun talk about?

25:21.561 --> 25:25.106
Why did he have to call you out
to talk to you?

25:25.190 --> 25:26.441
I was curious.

25:29.486 --> 25:31.446
Why do you ask questions when I don't?

25:35.825 --> 25:38.536
I didn't ask why
Yu-jin called you this morning.

25:38.620 --> 25:39.955
But why do you ask me?

25:42.082 --> 25:44.542
Is that why you're upset with me?

25:45.585 --> 25:46.878
No, it's not.

25:48.588 --> 25:50.882
- It looks like it is.
- Hey, one meter.

25:52.550 --> 25:54.010
- It is.
- One meter.

25:56.137 --> 25:59.432
I guess Ki-jun found out
that I'm Yu-jin's ex-boyfriend.

25:59.516 --> 26:01.810
It looked like he pestered her.

26:01.893 --> 26:04.938
She asked me to be careful,
so I told her I would.

26:05.021 --> 26:05.855
The end.

26:07.399 --> 26:09.943
Ki-jun is the kind of person
who holds grudges.

26:11.194 --> 26:12.153
Now it's your turn.

26:13.280 --> 26:14.322
What did Ki-jun say?

26:17.200 --> 26:20.578
He asked me if I was getting back at him

26:20.662 --> 26:23.832
by bringing you to my team knowing

26:24.332 --> 26:26.293
that you were his wife's ex-boyfriend.

26:26.376 --> 26:27.877
Why would I get back at him?

26:27.961 --> 26:32.299
Honestly, we didn't start this crazy act
to get back at anyone.

26:32.882 --> 26:33.717
Don't you agree?

26:33.800 --> 26:35.176
"Crazy act"?

26:36.886 --> 26:40.348
I dated a guy at work
and was humiliated once.

26:40.432 --> 26:42.684
Now I'm doing it again.
So it's a crazy act.

26:46.354 --> 26:47.856
I guess you're right.

26:52.986 --> 26:54.696
I'm not mad at you.

26:54.779 --> 26:56.990
I'm mad that I missed
the cold air moving south.

26:58.491 --> 26:59.868
I know.

27:01.745 --> 27:03.246
Okay, then. I'll get going first.

27:04.748 --> 27:06.416
Can I come to your place tonight?

27:08.168 --> 27:09.711
Bring a bottle of Pinot Noir.

27:09.794 --> 27:10.879
Okay!

27:16.885 --> 27:19.262
Get it together, Forecaster Lee!

27:19.846 --> 27:20.847
Yes, ma'am.

27:32.025 --> 27:34.361
Director Jin is really angry.

27:34.944 --> 27:36.571
I got scolded a lot.

27:36.654 --> 27:38.823
I didn't know she was so testy.

27:39.532 --> 27:40.992
Did I say anything?

27:43.912 --> 27:44.746
Right.

28:11.815 --> 28:13.817
Why don't you use the washing machine?

28:17.487 --> 28:19.155
Hasn't Ha-kyung called?

28:20.990 --> 28:24.536
People talk about
dogs having rights these days.

28:24.619 --> 28:28.331
You didn't even ask her opinion
before giving her information

28:28.415 --> 28:30.542
to a matchmaking service to grade her.

28:30.625 --> 28:32.919
That's so anachronistic and outdated.

28:34.421 --> 28:36.005
I didn't do it for me.

28:36.089 --> 28:38.716
If she marries a suitable man,

28:38.800 --> 28:41.803
her life will be easier,
and I'll be proud.

28:41.886 --> 28:43.179
Wouldn't that be nice?

28:43.847 --> 28:45.724
I devoted my whole life to raising her.

28:45.807 --> 28:47.308
A parent can expect that much.

28:47.976 --> 28:50.895
Mom, you're being greedy.

28:50.979 --> 28:52.313
Be quiet.

28:52.397 --> 28:53.690
Go do your work.

28:53.773 --> 28:57.277
I don't want to hear you whine
when the deadline is around the corner.

29:09.831 --> 29:11.124
Should I call her?

29:13.042 --> 29:16.087
No. I have my pride, you know.

29:21.301 --> 29:24.179
- Goodness.
- You drink it, Mom.

29:40.612 --> 29:41.988
Is something upsetting you?

29:42.989 --> 29:44.073
No.

29:44.157 --> 29:45.617
Did you fight with your husband?

29:46.284 --> 29:47.410
No, I didn't.

29:47.994 --> 29:49.496
What did you fight about? In-laws?

29:49.579 --> 29:51.915
Conflicting personalities?
Does he want to have a kid?

29:51.998 --> 29:53.082
I said we didn't fight.

29:55.919 --> 29:57.337
May I sit here?

29:57.420 --> 30:00.089
Gosh. Hello, Deputy Director Han.

30:00.173 --> 30:01.257
Enjoy your lunch.

30:03.426 --> 30:05.053
Why didn't you bring bulgogi?

30:05.136 --> 30:06.471
It looks really tasty today.

30:07.055 --> 30:09.224
Here. I'll give you mine.

30:16.564 --> 30:18.566
Yu-jin loves meat.

30:19.150 --> 30:21.236
But she never really gains weight.

30:21.319 --> 30:23.238
She must have won the genetic lottery.

30:23.321 --> 30:24.739
Sure.

30:24.823 --> 30:26.032
I guess so.

30:31.287 --> 30:32.956
Excuse me. I have to answer this.

30:37.252 --> 30:38.378
What are you doing?

30:39.796 --> 30:42.382
I'm saving your face.

30:42.465 --> 30:44.050
What? You don't like it?

30:44.133 --> 30:46.135
Should I make it obvious that we fought?

30:46.219 --> 30:47.554
We didn't fight.

30:48.179 --> 30:49.264
You were the one--

30:49.347 --> 30:51.140
What did you talk about with that jerk?

30:53.351 --> 30:54.561
Hello.

30:57.105 --> 31:00.275
That punk was so proud in front of me.

31:00.358 --> 31:02.569
He didn't feel sorry or guilty at all.

31:02.652 --> 31:04.529
He had no reason to be

31:04.612 --> 31:05.989
because it's over between us.

31:06.906 --> 31:08.658
Are you siding with him?

31:09.158 --> 31:10.827
You know I'm not.

31:10.910 --> 31:13.663
Anyway, don't run into him,
not even by chance.

31:13.746 --> 31:16.791
If you do, don't say hi to him.

31:16.875 --> 31:18.376
Don't even look at him, okay?

31:18.459 --> 31:20.587
Why don't you just tell me to quit my job?

31:21.754 --> 31:23.464
- Would you?
- Ki-jun.

31:23.548 --> 31:25.216
Reporters can work

31:25.300 --> 31:27.886
at the police station
or the prosecutors' office too.

31:28.469 --> 31:30.555
Why don't you move to another office?

31:30.638 --> 31:31.890
Come on.

31:31.973 --> 31:34.559
I can't leave Headquarters.
This is the perfect place to be.

31:35.268 --> 31:36.477
And listen to me, Yu-jin.

31:36.561 --> 31:39.230
You better stop talking back to me.

31:39.814 --> 31:41.524
I won't tolerate it anymore.

31:42.358 --> 31:44.235
What will you do if I don't stop?

31:44.944 --> 31:48.656
Anyway, don't ever lie to me again, okay?

31:48.740 --> 31:52.452
Gosh, I'm sorry.
That was an urgent call from home.

31:52.535 --> 31:53.703
Go on. The soup will get cold.

31:53.786 --> 31:55.872
- Okay.
- Eat up, Honey.

32:12.347 --> 32:13.264
Eat up.

32:14.390 --> 32:16.851
You're making me embarrassed
in front of her.

32:17.727 --> 32:20.271
You know, Yu-jin cares about me so much.

32:20.355 --> 32:21.314
I can see that.

32:21.397 --> 32:22.815
Goodness.

32:24.233 --> 32:25.443
It's so good.

32:40.917 --> 32:42.627
- One Americano, please.
- Sure.

32:43.795 --> 32:47.840
I heard Director Jin got furious
because a rookie corrected her.

32:48.758 --> 32:51.010
Come on. It wasn't that bad.

32:51.928 --> 32:53.304
I heard Kim Soo-jin

32:53.388 --> 32:56.224
from your team complaining about it.

32:56.307 --> 32:58.559
She said that Director Jin got mad

32:58.643 --> 33:01.062
and made the team
analyze ten years' worth of data.

33:01.854 --> 33:05.108
Don't you think it's wrong
to take it out on people like that?

33:05.191 --> 33:08.194
You must be having a hard time.

33:08.277 --> 33:10.405
It was nice when Director Choi was around.

33:10.488 --> 33:11.656
Well…

33:11.739 --> 33:13.783
I'm sure she'll do well.

33:14.409 --> 33:16.119
Here's your Americano.

33:16.744 --> 33:18.579
Every time I see her,

33:18.663 --> 33:20.999
I get scared
because she seems so heartless.

33:21.082 --> 33:23.584
- Right.
- Don't say that.

34:03.374 --> 34:04.542
Director Jin.

34:06.461 --> 34:07.837
Did you have lunch?

34:09.797 --> 34:11.591
Yes, I just did. What about you?

34:11.674 --> 34:13.718
We had kalguksu outside.

34:13.801 --> 34:16.054
I see. It must have been good.

34:17.847 --> 34:20.933
By the way, didn't you say
you were staying at the training center?

34:21.017 --> 34:21.851
Yes.

34:21.934 --> 34:25.146
Then how did you cross paths
with Director Jin this morning?

34:26.230 --> 34:27.565
The center is right there.

34:35.656 --> 34:36.824
I…

34:41.287 --> 34:43.372
This is Kim Soo-jin of Chief Team Two.

34:43.456 --> 34:45.750
It's about the rain echo
over Seoul just now.

34:46.501 --> 34:47.543
Echo?

34:50.046 --> 34:51.047
Please hold.

34:52.173 --> 34:54.967
Senior Forecaster Um,
it's the Metropolitan Office.

34:55.051 --> 34:56.969
They're saying the rain echo
over Seoul looks abnormal.

34:57.053 --> 34:59.055
- Could you take a look?
- What?

34:59.680 --> 35:00.681
Okay.

35:01.432 --> 35:02.517
What?

35:04.769 --> 35:08.689
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

35:09.440 --> 35:11.567
Why is this…

35:14.403 --> 35:17.865
- You went house-hunting in the morning?
- Yes, house-hunting.

35:19.408 --> 35:21.619
I guess the landlord was really busy,

35:21.702 --> 35:23.579
so he must have been available only then.

35:23.663 --> 35:24.580
Right?

35:24.664 --> 35:26.249
Yes, that's right.

35:26.332 --> 35:29.293
The landlord said he was busy. Yes.

35:32.672 --> 35:35.508
I'm sure you didn't go with him,
but you know so much.

35:41.055 --> 35:42.098
Right.

36:03.661 --> 36:05.788
Oh, my goodness.

36:11.460 --> 36:14.338
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

36:23.890 --> 36:24.974
It's raining.

36:27.935 --> 36:29.020
What should we do?

36:35.067 --> 36:35.902
Let's go!

36:38.613 --> 36:39.447
Hurry!

36:52.919 --> 36:55.379
Mom, did the weather forecast
say it'd rain?

36:55.463 --> 36:57.757
- Goodness.
- Oh, my gosh!

36:57.840 --> 36:59.300
No, it didn't.

37:00.343 --> 37:02.845
If it did,
I wouldn't have washed the comforters.

37:03.512 --> 37:04.764
Gosh, my back.

37:06.015 --> 37:07.141
Goodness.

37:07.934 --> 37:10.228
All hell will break loose.

37:16.317 --> 37:19.320
Hey, KMA! What are you doing?

37:19.403 --> 37:21.155
Why didn't you forecast this downpour?

37:21.239 --> 37:23.908
That's why they say
you never get anything right!

37:23.991 --> 37:24.992
Darn it!

37:29.538 --> 37:33.000
AUTOMATIC CONTROL PANEL

37:47.056 --> 37:48.182
What?

37:48.266 --> 37:49.684
- What's going on?
- Is it a blackout?

37:49.767 --> 37:51.102
- Damn it.
- Did the power go out?

37:51.185 --> 37:53.396
- What's going on?
- What's happening?

37:53.479 --> 37:55.273
- What?
- Is it a short circuit?

37:55.356 --> 37:56.816
- What?
- What's wrong?

37:56.899 --> 37:58.317
Find a candle.

37:58.401 --> 38:01.529
The entire building has no power.

38:01.612 --> 38:02.947
What are you going to do?

38:03.030 --> 38:04.490
Do you know how much damage this is?

38:05.157 --> 38:07.618
Quit forecasting weather
if you can't even predict rainfall.

38:07.702 --> 38:08.828
You're wasting our taxes.

38:08.911 --> 38:11.789
Are you going to pay for the damages?

38:14.250 --> 38:15.918
Why didn't you monitor this?

38:16.752 --> 38:18.170
I did.

38:18.254 --> 38:19.422
But…

38:21.382 --> 38:22.508
I missed it.

38:24.719 --> 38:26.345
Why? What were you doing?

38:29.223 --> 38:32.101
What's wrong with you these days?
Are you doing this on purpose?

38:32.184 --> 38:34.353
Director Jin,
I don't think you should say…

38:34.437 --> 38:36.981
Missing real-time monitoring
is a dereliction of duty.

38:37.064 --> 38:39.775
Depending on the extent of damage,
you may be dismissed.

38:42.486 --> 38:44.322
He would have had only five minutes

38:44.405 --> 38:45.948
if he hadn't missed the rain echo.

38:46.032 --> 38:48.659
The flooding couldn't have been
prevented anyway.

38:48.743 --> 38:50.328
The damage would have been smaller.

38:50.411 --> 38:52.496
How? It's raining 80mm per hour.

38:52.580 --> 38:53.789
That's enough.

38:53.873 --> 38:55.041
I'm sorry.

38:55.124 --> 38:56.917
It was my fault. So stop.

39:02.381 --> 39:03.549
I'm sorry.

39:04.675 --> 39:07.011
I missed the rain echo
because I was analyzing data.

39:09.472 --> 39:10.890
What are you saying?

39:13.309 --> 39:17.104
Honestly, isn't it impossible
to analyze ten years' worth of data

39:17.188 --> 39:18.522
in one day?

39:19.106 --> 39:21.400
If I had been monitoring
the radar instead of analyzing--

39:21.484 --> 39:23.527
You're terribly mistaken, Ms. Kim Soo-jin.

39:25.196 --> 39:27.490
Both data analysis and live monitoring

39:27.573 --> 39:30.034
are very important tasks that we must do.

39:31.035 --> 39:35.039
Missing one because of the other
is an excuse. Got it?

39:38.793 --> 39:40.002
It's not an excuse.

39:42.755 --> 39:44.632
I worked really hard to do well.

39:45.841 --> 39:46.926
Soo-jin.

39:47.009 --> 39:50.304
I'm really sorry
that I'm not very competent.

39:51.764 --> 39:56.185
Still, I tried really hard,
so please don't belittle my effort.

40:03.859 --> 40:05.653
What a great team we make.

40:20.876 --> 40:22.711
Director Jin and Senior Forecaster Um.

40:23.295 --> 40:25.172
The Director General wants to see you.

40:26.048 --> 40:27.133
Okay.

40:33.097 --> 40:35.558
As the stream swelled up,
the roads were flooded,

40:35.641 --> 40:38.018
twelve houses were submerged in water,

40:38.102 --> 40:41.105
and electricity was cut off
in an underground shopping mall.

40:41.188 --> 40:44.650
We'll have to wait and see
exactly how much damage it caused.

40:45.776 --> 40:46.777
Any casualties?

40:47.903 --> 40:49.029
Well…

40:50.030 --> 40:50.990
Are there casualties?

40:51.073 --> 40:54.160
Two workers went missing
during a regular inspection

40:54.243 --> 40:57.496
of drainage facilities at
the Anreung Rainwater Drainage Station.

41:00.666 --> 41:03.252
How is the search going?

41:03.335 --> 41:07.089
The paramedics and
the facility management are at work.

41:07.673 --> 41:09.717
We'll have to wait.

41:09.800 --> 41:11.135
This is killing me.

41:12.470 --> 41:13.512
I'm sorry.

41:14.889 --> 41:16.056
I missed it.

41:17.099 --> 41:18.142
It's my fault.

41:18.225 --> 41:21.604
I'll take full responsibility.

41:34.450 --> 41:37.578
- Why do you keep trying to look cool?
- What?

41:37.661 --> 41:40.206
In front of the team members
and the Director General,

41:40.289 --> 41:42.708
why did you say you'd take responsibility?

41:42.791 --> 41:45.169
Because I missed the real-time conditions.

41:45.252 --> 41:47.171
So why did you miss it?

41:47.755 --> 41:49.173
You said you were the Um Dong-han

41:49.256 --> 41:52.051
who could predict rain
just by smelling the east wind.

41:52.134 --> 41:54.803
How could you miss it
right before your eyes?

41:58.557 --> 41:59.725
What?

42:00.601 --> 42:02.937
Does it bother you that I'm your superior?

42:03.020 --> 42:05.564
No. How many times do I have to tell you--

42:05.648 --> 42:07.274
It doesn't matter.

42:07.358 --> 42:09.443
Since I'm the director of Chief Team Two,

42:09.527 --> 42:12.154
I'll take responsibility for your actions.

42:12.238 --> 42:14.573
So don't you dare say that you will.

42:16.033 --> 42:17.743
You're overstepping your authority.

42:37.179 --> 42:40.057
People think weather
and climate are the same,

42:40.683 --> 42:42.184
but they are actually different.

42:46.021 --> 42:49.024
While weather changes
from day to day like feelings,

42:49.108 --> 42:51.610
climate doesn't change easily

42:51.694 --> 42:54.029
because it's like
an innate personality of a person.

42:56.323 --> 42:58.784
When you don't know someone's personality,

42:58.867 --> 43:01.120
how could you flatter them?

43:06.208 --> 43:08.460
Are you siding with Director Jin?

43:08.544 --> 43:09.670
No.

43:10.379 --> 43:12.756
I'm telling you that I was wrong.

43:14.466 --> 43:18.053
While I only tried to predict the weather,

43:18.137 --> 43:20.764
Director Jin tried to analyze in detail

43:20.848 --> 43:23.309
how the current weather

43:23.392 --> 43:25.811
would affect people.

43:25.894 --> 43:28.439
Even if the same amount of rain
falls at the same time,

43:28.522 --> 43:31.233
the impact varies from region to region.

43:32.526 --> 43:34.945
When it rains 80mm per hour,

43:35.029 --> 43:36.822
Yeoksam will be fine,

43:36.905 --> 43:40.117
but Gangnam will be flooded
because the ground is lower.

43:42.620 --> 43:46.040
A forecast should be
able to reflect that as well.

43:46.123 --> 43:49.668
So it's important to analyze
as much data as possible.

43:54.882 --> 43:57.760
She asked us to analyze
ten years' worth of data

43:57.843 --> 43:59.803
to make consumer-centered forecasts,

44:00.804 --> 44:03.682
not producer-centered forecasts.

44:03.766 --> 44:06.435
So I was only thinking about performance,

44:07.144 --> 44:10.564
and she was thinking
of people who really needed

44:11.607 --> 44:12.858
a weather forecast.

44:17.071 --> 44:19.031
It's a little difficult.

44:21.116 --> 44:22.284
It is.

44:37.424 --> 44:39.510
What do you think of your team members?

44:40.302 --> 44:41.345
Pardon?

44:42.596 --> 44:44.807
Taking responsibility is important.

44:45.391 --> 44:46.642
But…

44:46.725 --> 44:49.436
you aren't the only one
who is working responsibly.

44:49.520 --> 44:52.231
We're all professionals at what we do.

44:54.775 --> 44:57.027
I'm saying we work
with a sense of responsibility.

45:00.572 --> 45:02.116
You trust us

45:02.199 --> 45:04.201
to do the work you assign us, don't you?

45:04.284 --> 45:07.371
Actually, I don't think
the team members have faith in me.

45:08.038 --> 45:10.541
They don't have confidence in my orders.

45:12.292 --> 45:15.337
It's not your orders
that we don't have confidence in.

45:15.421 --> 45:18.215
We don't have confidence in you

45:18.298 --> 45:20.217
because you aren't sure about your orders.

45:24.555 --> 45:25.389
Oh, right.

45:26.390 --> 45:27.599
Here.

45:27.683 --> 45:31.437
I analyzed data related to localized
heavy rain over the past ten years.

45:31.937 --> 45:33.939
In addition to
the main causes of heavy rain,

45:34.022 --> 45:36.775
I included cases such as
coupled upper and lower jet streams

45:36.859 --> 45:39.027
and lower convergence
and upper divergence.

45:39.111 --> 45:39.987
Take a look.

45:41.905 --> 45:42.948
Well…

45:43.574 --> 45:46.368
I finished what you asked me to do,
so I'll go home.

45:47.828 --> 45:48.912
Aren't you going home?

45:53.459 --> 45:54.877
Yes, Mother.

45:54.960 --> 45:56.670
Did the kids get soaked?

45:58.255 --> 46:00.090
I know.

46:02.593 --> 46:04.178
Exactly.

46:04.845 --> 46:08.182
I work at the KMA,
but my kids get rained on.

46:31.705 --> 46:33.373
Hi, Yu-jin. It's me.

46:34.166 --> 46:36.710
I'm on my way out. Wait for me.

46:37.336 --> 46:40.088
What do you want for dinner, baby?

46:40.172 --> 46:43.133
Oh, tteokbokki.

46:43.217 --> 46:45.344
Okay. I'll buy you everything.

46:48.805 --> 46:50.265
No problem.

46:59.900 --> 47:01.527
- Good luck.
- Good work.

47:04.196 --> 47:06.490
- Are you going home?
- Yes. You?

47:06.573 --> 47:07.407
I will.

47:07.491 --> 47:09.952
Everyone left. I'm the last one.

47:19.461 --> 47:24.174
ANREUNG RAINWATER DRAINAGE STATION

47:24.258 --> 47:25.968
EMERGENCY RESCUE CONTROL
ON-SITE COMMAND

47:29.513 --> 47:31.181
THIRD PRESS BRIEFING

47:31.265 --> 47:33.850
ANREUNG DRAINAGE STATION
SEARCH FOR MISSING PEOPLE

47:33.934 --> 47:35.561
MISSING WORKERS: 2 PEOPLE

47:51.243 --> 47:53.036
Do you see anything?

47:53.120 --> 47:54.705
- Over there.
- Shine the light here.

47:54.788 --> 47:56.540
- Search over there too.
- Okay.

47:56.623 --> 47:58.375
We don't have much time.

47:58.458 --> 48:00.669
- We need to hurry up.
- We should check there.

48:01.712 --> 48:04.339
- I think they might be there.
- Shine the light over there.

48:26.445 --> 48:28.488
DANGER

48:28.572 --> 48:29.906
What are you doing here?

48:30.532 --> 48:31.450
Hey.

48:31.533 --> 48:34.077
I couldn't go to sleep anyway.

48:34.161 --> 48:36.496
If I lurk around,

48:36.580 --> 48:39.791
they'll think that
I have some moral sense at least.

48:41.001 --> 48:43.170
- What about the workers?
- No news yet.

48:54.973 --> 48:56.224
Thank you.

49:16.953 --> 49:20.290
The person you are trying
to reach is unavailable…

49:20.374 --> 49:21.833
She's not picking up.

49:24.378 --> 49:27.172
Which one will she like more?

50:07.129 --> 50:09.589
RESTRICTED
KEEP OUT

50:10.841 --> 50:12.718
We found them!

50:12.801 --> 50:14.678
They're both okay here!

50:15.804 --> 50:17.389
- Here.
- Careful.

50:17.472 --> 50:19.182
- Where?
- Please let it down carefully.

50:20.016 --> 50:21.685
Are you okay, sir?

50:21.768 --> 50:24.438
- Can you move?
- Are you okay?

50:25.147 --> 50:27.357
Over here. Move them here.

50:27.441 --> 50:30.068
- A little more. Watch your hands!
- Are they conscious?

50:30.652 --> 50:32.112
Thank goodness.

50:32.946 --> 50:34.698
What a relief.

50:38.535 --> 50:40.120
Did you have dinner?

50:40.704 --> 50:42.080
No. You?

50:43.248 --> 50:45.125
Let's go and have some hot soup.

50:47.169 --> 50:48.879
Bring them here!

51:04.227 --> 51:05.061
What?

51:06.104 --> 51:07.439
Did you leave home?

51:11.026 --> 51:12.402
Yes.

51:13.403 --> 51:14.780
It's a long story.

51:22.913 --> 51:24.331
Doors opening.

51:28.126 --> 51:29.419
Wait.

51:30.253 --> 51:31.630
Thank you.

51:33.173 --> 51:35.675
- What floor are you going to?
- Twelfth floor, please.

51:36.760 --> 51:37.844
Doors closing.

51:50.357 --> 51:52.150
I guess you live right above me.

51:52.234 --> 51:53.693
Are you apartment number 1301?

51:53.777 --> 51:55.111
Or 1302?

51:56.196 --> 51:57.572
I'm 1302.

51:58.240 --> 51:59.616
I see.

52:02.285 --> 52:04.621
We're neighbors.

52:05.288 --> 52:07.332
My sister lives in 1201.

52:12.629 --> 52:14.005
Bye.

52:27.102 --> 52:28.728
What?

52:41.658 --> 52:42.951
What?

52:43.451 --> 52:44.661
Did she change it?

53:38.381 --> 53:39.758
Who could that be?

53:54.022 --> 53:55.357
Hello.

53:55.440 --> 53:57.025
Hi. What is it?

53:57.108 --> 53:58.777
I told you

53:58.860 --> 54:00.820
my sister lived downstairs.

54:00.904 --> 54:02.155
Yes. And?

54:02.238 --> 54:04.074
Well…

54:04.908 --> 54:07.494
- please take these.
- What for?

54:08.078 --> 54:10.163
Could you please hang on to these?

54:10.246 --> 54:13.416
She changed the passcode
and she won't pick up her phone.

54:13.500 --> 54:15.377
Well, then…

54:15.460 --> 54:17.462
Maybe you can ask the security guard.

54:18.171 --> 54:19.255
I know.

54:19.339 --> 54:20.840
I checked the security office,

54:20.924 --> 54:22.842
but he's on patrol.

54:23.343 --> 54:25.387
These are kimchi and bulgogi

54:25.470 --> 54:28.932
my aged mother made for her daughter
in this hot weather.

54:29.015 --> 54:30.266
What if they go bad?

54:31.309 --> 54:33.812
They're too heavy for me
to bring back home.

54:35.855 --> 54:37.399
Do me a favor.

54:37.482 --> 54:38.692
Please?

54:40.026 --> 54:41.319
We're neighbors.

54:41.403 --> 54:42.487
Right.

54:47.742 --> 54:50.495
Why don't you wait for their dad?

54:50.578 --> 54:52.580
He'll be late because of dinner at work.

54:52.664 --> 54:55.041
- Is that right?
- Thank you, Mother.

54:55.125 --> 54:56.459
No problem.

54:56.543 --> 54:58.336
- Good night.
- Okay.

54:58.420 --> 54:59.963
- Good night.
- All right, pumpkin.

55:00.046 --> 55:01.673
Good boy. Let's go.

55:01.756 --> 55:03.091
- Good night.
- Bye.

55:03.174 --> 55:04.884
- Let's go.
- Okay.

55:04.968 --> 55:06.428
- Take care.
- Bye.

55:06.511 --> 55:08.263
- Go.
- Let's go.

55:08.346 --> 55:09.264
Okay.

55:09.889 --> 55:11.558
Are you sleepy?

55:13.143 --> 55:14.686
Dad!

55:15.520 --> 55:16.688
- Hey.
- What?

55:17.397 --> 55:19.232
You're here early.

55:19.315 --> 55:21.192
You said you were having dinner.

55:22.068 --> 55:23.862
I didn't go.

55:24.946 --> 55:26.031
Why not?

55:27.699 --> 55:30.326
I had some stuff to think about.

55:32.120 --> 55:33.872
What's wrong?

55:35.373 --> 55:36.666
What is it?

55:38.501 --> 55:39.544
Honey.

55:41.129 --> 55:44.632
Can I take the Grade Five
technical exam again?

55:45.508 --> 55:46.342
What?

55:47.719 --> 55:49.679
What about your work?

55:53.349 --> 55:55.477
I'm thinking of taking a year off.

55:55.560 --> 55:56.686
Can I do that?

55:59.939 --> 56:01.024
Well…

56:03.276 --> 56:04.986
No.

56:05.570 --> 56:09.574
People may say that it's okay
to make mistakes,

56:09.657 --> 56:12.035
but we should never make mistakes.

56:12.118 --> 56:13.745
You're right about that,

56:14.496 --> 56:16.998
but we shouldn't say
we'd take responsibility.

56:18.083 --> 56:20.960
Predicting and forecasting

56:21.044 --> 56:24.255
the uncertain future weather diligently

56:24.339 --> 56:25.882
is our job.

56:26.883 --> 56:29.135
But assuming responsibility

56:29.219 --> 56:31.221
for the things that may happen?

56:31.304 --> 56:32.680
That's absurd.

56:34.557 --> 56:37.894
You were the one who said it first.

56:37.977 --> 56:39.979
That's because I made a mistake.

56:40.480 --> 56:43.066
I'll be responsible
for the mistake I made.

56:43.733 --> 56:45.193
That's what I'm saying.

56:46.277 --> 56:49.489
"Our one little mistake can kill someone

56:49.572 --> 56:52.117
or make someone lose his entire fortune."

56:52.659 --> 56:54.828
"Stay alert all the time

56:54.911 --> 56:57.288
and look for signs and clues."

56:57.372 --> 56:58.414
Guess who said it.

56:58.498 --> 57:00.917
I don't know. Who said it?

57:02.460 --> 57:05.797
Do you remember what you said
when you trained Grade Five officers

57:05.880 --> 57:07.549
eight years ago?

57:07.632 --> 57:10.343
"All systems
responsible for national safety

57:10.426 --> 57:12.011
start with weather forecasting."

57:12.846 --> 57:15.598
"Therefore, a forecaster must have
a sense of duty first,

57:15.682 --> 57:17.725
and a sense of duty second."

57:19.644 --> 57:22.897
If I hadn't taken that class,
I wouldn't be struggling now.

57:22.981 --> 57:25.692
I would have been on the track
for a senior position.

57:28.820 --> 57:31.239
Did I tell you to be fooled by that?

57:31.823 --> 57:33.158
It was your choice.

57:43.751 --> 57:45.837
So what happened to you since then?

57:46.963 --> 57:48.548
What's gotten into you?

57:50.967 --> 57:52.677
Darn it.

57:54.929 --> 57:56.139
I think…

57:57.849 --> 58:00.351
I lost some kind of motivation.

58:01.019 --> 58:02.020
What?

58:02.687 --> 58:06.024
For what? For what cause?

58:06.691 --> 58:10.111
For whom?
You need to have something like that.

58:13.865 --> 58:17.285
I don't have that anymore.

58:40.975 --> 58:45.230
Please wait.
Your transaction has been processed.

58:51.110 --> 58:52.987
Please accept your cash.

58:53.071 --> 58:54.572
Thank you very much.

58:57.909 --> 59:01.538
Thank you for using our services.
Please make sure you do not leave…

59:01.621 --> 59:04.374
IMI MOTEL

59:21.891 --> 59:23.434
Be careful.

59:23.518 --> 59:26.020
Be careful. Here.

59:26.104 --> 59:28.231
My goodness. Please wait here.

59:28.314 --> 59:29.899
- Senior Forecaster Um.
- Yes.

59:29.983 --> 59:31.484
What's your home address?

59:31.568 --> 59:35.196
Gangwon Province, Gangneung, Science…

59:35.905 --> 59:38.116
Your home in Seoul, not Gangwon Office.

59:38.199 --> 59:39.701
- I'll call a driver.
- What?

59:40.243 --> 59:41.119
Home?

59:43.288 --> 59:45.206
My home is…

59:46.583 --> 59:48.418
I have no home.

59:49.043 --> 59:52.797
Gangwon… It's the KMA.

59:52.880 --> 59:56.134
All right. I'll go to the KMA.

59:57.552 --> 59:58.803
The KMA…

01:00:31.002 --> 01:00:32.170
Mr. Lee Si-woo?

01:00:36.799 --> 01:00:38.760
- Watch the steps.
- Okay.

01:00:50.938 --> 01:00:52.565
We have different personalities,

01:00:53.566 --> 01:00:55.318
different principles,

01:00:55.401 --> 01:00:57.987
and different wounds.

01:00:58.071 --> 01:00:59.572
So it is only natural

01:01:00.323 --> 01:01:02.367
for the atmosphere to become unstable

01:01:02.450 --> 01:01:06.371
and an abnormal climate event
to appear when we meet.

01:01:06.454 --> 01:01:08.289
Why are you…

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:09.999
Why are you…

01:01:11.501 --> 01:01:12.752
here?

01:01:18.424 --> 01:01:25.431
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

01:01:29.185 --> 01:01:32.689
IMI MOTEL

01:02:11.644 --> 01:02:13.438
Your sister just called.

01:02:13.521 --> 01:02:15.565
Your mother is very sick.

01:02:15.648 --> 01:02:17.900
It seems pretty serious.

01:02:17.984 --> 01:02:20.486
She's not the type who'd listen to us.

01:02:20.570 --> 01:02:22.280
I'm okay. You can go in first.

01:02:24.323 --> 01:02:26.617
You should make an investment

01:02:26.701 --> 01:02:28.619
if you want to date a young guy.

01:02:28.703 --> 01:02:31.581
- Don't tell me you met Director Jin.
- What the…

01:02:31.664 --> 01:02:34.041
My mind has been racing.

01:02:37.003 --> 01:02:38.337
Let's reconsider this.

01:02:39.046 --> 01:02:40.298
You and me.

01:02:41.174 --> 01:02:45.553
Subtitle translation by: Soo-hyun Yang
